    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90034.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 31,
    "turn_text": "In some ways, I'm sure it'd be uncomfortable. I remember the Washington Post article that described me as this most loyal cabinet member. I am proud of the work that we did, and I am deeply grateful to the four years that he gave me. I mean, who dreamed that This kid would get to be the CI director in the secondary state for America. So, yeah, he's someone who I have respect for the things that we did for those four years. And so, you know, I expected to be a little uncomfortable for him too, right? We worked so closely together and we delivered such good outcomes for the American people. But that discomfort would not deter you. If you think you're the right person and everything else lines up, you ought to go do it and then let the American people sort it out.",
